    "description": "Fixed sealed-sender certificate data: the trust roots configured in signal-cli v0.14.7, libsignal v0.99.1's built-in KNOWN_SERVER_CERTIFICATES table, and the three fixed SenderCertificate fixtures in libsignal's sealed_sender.rs unit tests. All public keys are 33-byte serialized Curve25519 keys (0x05 prefix). Signatures are libsignal XEd25519 (see spec/crypto/xeddsa.md); the three known-server-certificate signatures also appear as verify vectors in xeddsa.json. Upstream asserts: each known server certificate validates under its listed trust root, and each sender-certificate fixture validates under the test trust root at time 31336 ms. The outcomes at times 31337 and 31338 are NOT asserted upstream for these fixtures; they follow from the expiry rule in sealed_sender.rs (a certificate is expired only when the validation time is strictly greater than 'expires') and are marked 'derived_from_rule'. The spec agent did not re-verify the signatures independently. See spec/protocol/sealed-sender.md.",
